{{- /* Package-doc partial: emits the `// Package X ...` block
       immediately preceding the `package X` declaration.

       Surface lists are deliberately scoped to "what the auto-test
       in this package exercises end-to-end against the generated
       stub" — Returns / Func / Faults / FaultX / RetrySchedule /
       FaultForPartition / Yields / FaultMiss / OnRecord / LastCall /
       CallCount / AssertCalledOnce / Reset / ResetCalls. The
       broader runtime [stub.MethodStub] / Recorder API
       (FaultsWithProbability, FaultsFor, FaultsUntil, FaultsWhen,
       SetFault, Latency, Times, TimesAtLeast, AssertCalledN,
       AssertNotCalled, Filter, First, Any, All, WaitForN, WaitFor,
       NewGate) is inherited via embedding and tested directly in
       go.thesmos.sh/testkit/stub — listing it here would advertise
       coverage we don't own. */ -}}
{{- define "package-doc" -}}
{{- $stub := .StubName -}}
{{- $iface := .Spec.QualifiedType -}}
// Package {{ .PackageName }} provides {{ $stub }}, a configurable test double
// for [{{ $iface }}] generated by `testkit stub`.
//
// # Usage
//
//	func TestThing(t *testing.T) {
//	    s := {{ .PackageName }}.New{{ $stub }}{{ .TestTypeArgs }}(t)
//	    s.OnX.Returns(...)        // configure a fixed return
//	    s.OnX.Func(fn)            // intercept dispatch with a closure
//	    s.OnX.Faults(err, n)      // inject a counter-based fault
//	    // ... call code under test ...
//	    call := s.OnX.LastCall(t) // assert recorded args + results
//	}
//
// # Dispatch contract
//
// Every method runs the same priority chain and records the call
// exactly once on whichever path fires:
//
//	SleepLatency  →  fault?  →  Func?  →  Returns?  →  FailUnexpectedCall
//
// Recording happens on every path (so OnRecord, CallCount, and
// LastCall observe configured AND unconfigured dispatches uniformly)
// except under [{{ $stub }}BenchMode] which disables the recorder
// entirely for allocation-free benchmarks.
//
// # Stub-level options
//
// Pass to [New{{ $stub }}] as the variadic opts:
//
//   - [{{ $stub }}Strict]         — unconfigured calls fatal the test.
//   - [{{ $stub }}DelegateTo]     — wrap a real implementation as the default Func.
//   - [{{ $stub }}WithClock]      — virtual time for Latency, FaultsFor, timestamps.
//   - [{{ $stub }}WithRandSource] — deterministic source for FaultsWithProbability.
//   - [{{ $stub }}BenchMode]      — disable recording for zero-alloc dispatch.
//
// Per-method [Func] overrides may also be installed at construction
// via the With{{ .Spec.Interface.Name }}<Method> options.
//
// # Per-method API
//
// Each [{{ $stub }}].OnX field is a *{{ $stub }}<Method>. The auto-test
// in this package verifies:
//
//   - Func / Returns / Faults / Fault<Sentinel> / RetrySchedule /
//     FaultForPartition / Yields / YieldsError / FaultMiss helpers
//     emitted per method's shape and directives.
//   - OnRecord, LastCall, CallCount, AssertCalledOnce — the
//     observation surface used by the auto-test.
//   - ResetCalls clearing recordings AND preserving Func / Returns
//     / Faults state across the reset.
//   - Times / TimesAtLeast cleanup verification — mismatched
//     expectations fail the test at tb.Cleanup time.
//
// The remaining runtime [stub.MethodStub] + Recorder API (Latency,
// AssertCalledN, AssertNotCalled, Filter, First, Any, All, WaitForN,
// WaitFor, NewGate, FaultsFor, FaultsUntil, FaultsWhen, ...) is
// inherited via embedding; consult the runtime package for those
// behaviors and tests.
{{ end -}}
